[17592186051362 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186051363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051362 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186051364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051362 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186051365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051362 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186051366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051362 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186051367 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051362 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051362 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051362 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bbeb8dbc-dca5-5d86-981e-fbd5f85769d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051363 #edb/ref 1080 "a, b, c ∉ S" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051363 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051363 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8f216052-b042-5650-b7c1-f56d813bb264" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051364 #edb/ref 1080 "d, e ∈ S" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051364 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051364 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "973501b7-20a2-561e-9cdb-a2e67572d6e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051365 #edb/ref 1080 "$a, b, c ∉ S$ and $d, e ∈ S$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051365 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051365 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b1434d4a-3e58-5dfd-8acb-d5d13c5bb75e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051366 #edb/ref 1080 "$a, b ∈ S$ and $c, d, e ∉ S$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051366 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051366 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cf72a39d-e96c-59f7-b87e-82bf7b8787d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051367 #edb/ref 1080 "$a, b, c ∈ S$ and $d, e ∉ S$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051367 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051367 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fb8f170e-df2c-5a3b-bfe7-914ce60157f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054425 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13134" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054425 #edb/ref 1071 "List the elements of the following set:\n$A = \\big\\{a, c,3, \\{c,3 \\}, \\emptyset, \\{\\emptyset\\}\\big\\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054425 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "16e0f524-49b5-549d-8e60-8597379c4350" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054425 #edb/ref 1074 "The elements of the set $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\na, \\quad c, \\quad 3, \\quad \\{c,3\\}, \\quad \\emptyset, \\quad \\{\\emptyset\\}\n$$\n\n**Watch Out!**\n\n- The elements $c,3$, and $\\{c,3\\}$ are three separate entities. The first two are the elements $c$ and $3$, and the third is a set *containing* these two elements.\n- The elements $\\emptyset$ and $\\{\\emptyset \\}$ are also separate entities. The first one is the empty set (i.e., the set containing no elements), while the second is a set that contains the empty set." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054426 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13135" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054426 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is **not** a set?\n\n1. $\\{2, 4, 6 \\}$\n2. $\\{\\{2 \\}, \\{4, 6 \\} \\}$\n3. $2, 4, 6$\n4. $\\emptyset$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054426 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "046f7284-3715-555c-bdc9-c108db061205" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054426 #edb/ref 1074 "A set is a collection of elements listed between two braces (curly brackets). However, note that the null set (the set that does not contain any elements) can be written as either $\\{\\}$ or $\\emptyset$.\n\n- $\\{2, 4, 6 \\}$ is a set. The elements are $2$, $4$, and $6$, and they are listed between two braces.\n- $\\{\\{2 \\}, \\{4, 6 \\} \\}$ is a set. The elements are $\\{2 \\}$ and $\\{4, 6 \\}$, and are listed between the two outermost braces.\n- $2, 4, 6$ is *not* a set. The numbers $2$, $4$, and $6$ are *not* listed between two braces.\n- $\\emptyset$ is the empty set. Therefore, it is a set.\n\nIn conclusion, only III is not a set." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054427 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13136" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054427 #edb/ref 1071 "Write the following statement using element notation:\n\n$\\qquad$ $1$ and $2$ are elements of a set $S$, but $3$, $4$, and $5$ are not." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054427 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5404d545-570b-53d7-b16a-b23a371d4abd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054427 #edb/ref 1074 "If $a$ is an element of $S$, we write $a \\in S$. Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S$, we write $a \\notin S$.\n\n- Since $1$ and $2$ are elements of $S$, we write $1,2 \\in S$.\n- Since $3$, $4$, and $5$ are *not* elements of $S$, we write $3,4,5 \\notin S$.\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$$\n1,2 \\in S\\quad \\textrm{and}\\quad 3,4,5 \\notin S\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054428 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13137" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054428 #edb/ref 1071 "Express the following sets using an ellipsis:\n\n- The set $X$ of all positive integers greater than or equal to $10$\n- The set $Y$ of integers less than zero\n- The set $A$ of all natural numbers greater than $5$ and less than $5\\, 005$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054428 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0684e366-bcf4-5b08-8eae-6600a88e2920" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054428 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that an ellipsis means \"and so on up to\" if it's followed by a specific element, or \"and so on\" if not.\n\n- To express the set $X$, we start with the first positive integer greater than or equal to $10$, which is $10$. The next integer is $11$, the one after that is $12$, and so on, which we denote with an ellipsis:\n$X = \\{10, 11, 12, \\ldots \\}$\n- To express the set $Y$, we start with the first integer less than zero, which is $-1$. The next integer less than zero is $-2$, the one after that is $-3$, and so on, which we denote with an ellipsis:\n$Y = \\{-1, -2, -3, \\ldots \\}$\nHowever, note that it is conventional to write a set of numbers from least to greatest, just like is shown on the number line. Writing the elements of $Y$ from least to greatest, we have\n$Y = \\{\\ldots, -3, -2, -1\\}$.\n- To express the set $A$, we start with the first positive integer greater than $5$, which is $6$. The next integer is $7$, the one after that is $8$, and so on up to $5\\, 004$ (the largest integer less than $5\\, 005$). So, we have\n$A = \\{6, 7, 8, \\ldots, 5004\\}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054848 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186054965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054848 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186054970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054848 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054848 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying the Elements of a Set" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054848 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054848 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "33551349-bb39-5a79-bf56-a4df753201ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054849 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186054964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054849 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186054971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054849 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054849 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Non-Sets" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054849 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054849 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "de59db4d-82d5-5bad-a559-bf5396375355" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054850 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186054972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054850 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186054973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054850 #edb/ref 1039 "Using Element Notation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054850 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054850 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "900f0d3d-6a5c-53b2-b987-eee1a8963b6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054851 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054851 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054851 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186054966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054851 #